===Television debates===
One debate took place before the first round, on 5 May, chaired by [[Krzysztof Ziemiec]] and aired on [[TVP 1]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.press.pl/newsy/telewizja/pokaz/48706,Krzysztof-Ziemiec-poprowadzi-debate-dziesieciu-kandydatow|language=pl|title=Krzysztof Ziemiec poprowadzi debatę dziesięciu kandydatów|agency=Press|date=5 May 2015|access-date=29 May 2015}}</ref> Ten candidates attended the debate, while President Komorowski declined to appear.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.thenews.pl/1/2/Artykul/205825,Candidates-debate-on-TV-prior-to-presidential-elections|agency=Radio Poland|title=Candidates debate on TV prior to presidential elections|date=5 May 2015|access-date=29 May 2015|archive-date=29 May 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150529115327/http://www.thenews.pl/1/2/Artykul/205825,Candidates-debate-on-TV-prior-to-presidential-elections|url-status=dead}}</ref>

Two debates took place before the second round, the first chaired by [[Dorota Gawryluk]] and by [[Krzysztof Ziemiec]] on 17 May,<ref>{{cite news|url=http://pl.blastingnews.com/polityka/2015/05/starcie-kandydatow-na-prezydenta-w-debacie-wyborczej-00399493.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150529113829/http://pl.blastingnews.com/polityka/2015/05/starcie-kandydatow-na-prezydenta-w-debacie-wyborczej-00399493.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=29 May 2015|language=pl|agency=Blasting News|title=Starcie kandydatów na prezydenta w debacie wyborczej|date=18 May 2015|access-date=29 May 2015}}</ref> and the second on 21 May by [[TVN (Poland)|TVN]], chaired by [[Monika Olejnik]], [[Bogdan Rymanowski]] and [[Justyna Pochanke]]. In both of these, the candidates also had the opportunity to pose questions to the other.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2015-05-20/polish-debate-pits-presidential-rivals-in-race-too-close-to-call|agency=Bloomberg|title=Polish Ballot Too Close to Call as Presidential Debate Looms|date=20 May 2015|access-date=29 May 2015|last=Skolimowski|first=Piotr}}</ref> Komorowski was generally regarded by the Polish press and political analysts to have won the first of the second-round debates.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2015-05-17/polish-president-wins-debate-in-bid-to-revamp-election-campaign|agency=Bloomberg|title=Polish President Revives Election Campaign With Debate Win|first=Piotr|last=Skolimowski|date=17 May 2015|access-date=29 May 2015}}</ref> The second debate was considered to be less decisive.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.thenews.pl/1/9/Artykul/207642,Duda-and-Komorowski-end-TV-debate|title=Duda and Komorowski participate in TV debate|agency=Radio Poland|date=21 May 2015|access-date=29 May 2015|archive-date=29 May 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150529111712/http://www.thenews.pl/1/9/Artykul/207642,Duda-and-Komorowski-end-TV-debate|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/europe/polish-president-challenger-face-off-in-last-debate/2015/05/21/9d735a10-ffe4-11e4-8c77-bf274685e1df_story.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150529112621/http://www.washingtonpost.com/world/europe/polish-president-challenger-face-off-in-last-debate/2015/05/21/9d735a10-ffe4-11e4-8c77-bf274685e1df_story.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=29 May 2015|newspaper=The Washington Post|title=Polish president, challenger face off in last debate|date=21 May 2015|access-date=29 May 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2015-05-21/polish-challenger-duda-carries-last-debate-before-president-vote|agency=Bloomberg|title=No Knockout in Polish Presidential Debate as Election Nears|first=Piotr|last=Skolimowski|date=21 May 2015|access-date=29 May 2015}}</ref>

