==Results==
Duda took a narrow first-place finish over Komorowski in the first round of the election on 10 May 2015, forcing the incumbent into a runoff. The result was described as a surprise, as the Komorowski camp and many political observers expected him to perform better or perhaps win outright.<ref name="stunner"/><ref name="unpredictable"/><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-poland-vote-president-idUSKBN0NU0RX20150510|work=Reuters|title=Polish president suffers shock reverse in first round vote: exit poll|date=10 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2015-05-10/poles-hand-president-komorowski-shock-defeat-in-first-round-vote|agency=Bloomberg|title=Poles Hand President Komorowski Shock Defeat in First-Round|date=10 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015}}</ref> [[Paweł Kukiz]], who finished third in the first round of voting, declined to endorse either Duda or Komorowski, instead offering to moderate a debate between the two candidates.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.thenews.pl/1/9/Artykul/206654,Kukiz-invites-Komorowski-Duda-for-presidential-debate|agency=Radio Poland|title=Kukiz invites Komorowski, Duda, for presidential debate|date=13 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015}}{{Dead link|date=February 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref> Komorowski declined to participate, and the debate was never held.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.thenews.pl/1/9/Artykul/207500,Kukizled-presidential-debate-cancelled|agency=Radio Poland|title=Kukiz-led presidential debate cancelled|date=21 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015|archive-date=28 May 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150528184513/http://www.thenews.pl/1/9/Artykul/207500,Kukizled-presidential-debate-cancelled|url-status=dead}}</ref>

In the second round of the election on 24 May, Duda unseated Komorowski in what was until [[2020 Polish presidential election|2020]] the closest presidential election since Poland became a democracy.<ref name="late">{{cite news|url=http://www.warsawvoice.pl/WVpage/pages/article.php/31819/news|work=The Warsaw Voice|title=Andrzej Duda wins Poland's presidential election – late poll results|date=24 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.eho.com.hr/news/andrzej-duda-wins-polands-presidential-election/9939.aspx|title=Andrzej Duda wins Poland's presidential election|agency=EHO|date=26 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015}}</ref> He defeated the incumbent by a margin of approximately three percentage points, according to official results.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.aljazeera.com/news/2015/05/duda-wins-polands-presidential-election-150525164751445.html|publisher=Al Jazeera|title=Conservative Duda wins Poland's presidential vote|date=25 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015}}</ref>
