==Reactions==
Komorowski said after the release of the exit poll that it was important to respect the result of the vote.<ref name="late"/> He conceded defeat that evening and wished Duda "a successful presidency".<ref name="concedes">{{cite news|url=http://www.avaz.ba/clanak/179467/poland-election-komorowski-concedes-defeat-to-duda|work=Dnevi avaz|title=Poland election: Komorowski concedes defeat to Duda|date=25 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015}}</ref>

Duda hailed his victory as a vote for change.<ref name="concedes"/> His campaign manager said the election showed that the [[Law and Justice (Poland)|Law and Justice]] bloc could win [[2015 Polish parliamentary election|parliamentary elections]] scheduled for autumn,<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.dpa-international.com/news/international/polish-right-wing-party-eyes-fall-electionsafter-dudas-victory-a-45370968.html|agency=Deutsche Presse-Agentur|title=Polish right-wing party eyes fall elections after Duda's victory|date=25 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015|first=Eva|last=Krafczyk|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150528181453/http://www.dpa-international.com/news/international/polish-right-wing-party-eyes-fall-electionsafter-dudas-victory-a-45370968.html|archive-date=28 May 2015|url-status=dead}}</ref> something that the party achieved.

Many world leaders, including [[United States]] President [[Barack Obama]],<ref>{{cite news|url=http://thenews.pl/1/10/Artykul/208077,White-House-congratulates-Presidentelect-Duda|agency=Radio Poland|title=White House congratulates President-elect Duda|date=26 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015|archive-date=28 May 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150528184000/http://thenews.pl/1/10/Artykul/208077,White-House-congratulates-Presidentelect-Duda|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[Germany|German]] Chancellor [[Angela Merkel]],<ref>{{cite news|language=pl|url=http://www.polskieradio.pl/5/3/Artykul/1450023,Kanclerz-Angela-Merkel-prezydent-Niemiec-i-szef-PE-gratuluja-Andrzejowi-Dudzie|title=Kanclerz Angela Merkel, prezydent Niemiec i szef PE gratulują Andrzejowi Dudzie|date=25 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015|website=PolskieRadio.pl|archive-date=28 May 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150528211921/http://www.polskieradio.pl/5/3/Artykul/1450023,Kanclerz-Angela-Merkel-prezydent-Niemiec-i-szef-PE-gratuluja-Andrzejowi-Dudzie|url-status=dead}}</ref> and [[Russia]]n President [[Vladimir Putin]],<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.ndtv.com/world-news/vladimir-putin-wants-constructive-poland-ties-after-duda-presidential-win-765976|publisher=NDTV|title=Vladimir Putin Wants 'Constructive' Poland Ties After Duda Presidential Win|date=25 May 2015|access-date=28 May 2015}}</ref> congratulated Duda on his victory.

